# platform.rp2350_touch_lcd_154.audio

The Waveshare RP2350 LCD 1.54 family's Speaker and Microphone: the board's
ES8311 codec, its DAC through an NS4150B amplifier to the speaker connector
and its ADC from the analog microphone, over one mm.audio.es8311 Codec that
both share. rp2350_lcd_154 binds it, and rp2350_touch_lcd_154 inherits the
binding.

The codec is at 0x18 on I2C1, SDA GP6 and SCL GP7, shared with the IMU and on
the touch model the touch controller; configuring that bus is idempotent, so
no provider depends on another having been initialised first. Its I2S link is
data out GP1, data in GP2, bit clock GP4, and word clock GP5, the word clock on
the GPIO after the bit clock as a PIO transmitter's side-set needs, with
sixteen-bit slots.

Waveshare's firmware runs the codec as the I2S master, clocked from a 6.144
MHz MCLK the RP2350 generates on GP3. This provider runs it as the slave
mm.mcu's I2S facility drives instead, with the codec's master clock taken
from the bit clock, so GP3 is not a clock here: both devices hold it low
before initialising the codec, rather than leave the MCLK input floating.

The Speaker adds the amplifier to the ES8311 Output: GP0, NS_MODE, low until
start, raised once the codec's port is unmuted, and lowered again before the
codec mutes on stop or sleep, so neither edge of the amplifier hears a
half-configured codec. The Microphone is the ES8311 Input, reading the left
slot, where the codec's default ADCDAT selection puts the ADC in both slots,
at the PGA's thirty decibels.

The link runs over the Pico platform's PIO I2S. None of this is qualified on
hardware.
